atlas optimization-native-retirement

architecture native-ratchet
  canonical_name NativeRatchet
  family optimization
  domain Optimization / Estate governance
  layer governance
  semantic_question Is the JS and script estate shrinking toward C over YAFF/CUE, and is anything installed as a program still a packed JS runtime?
  purpose Turn the retirement of the .mjs estate into a one-way door: every win lowers a budget, and nothing (person, Claude or Codex) can grow the estate back without a reviewed edit to the budgets
  maturity measured
  owns NativeRatchetBudget
  publishes NativeRatchetMeasure
  source_path scripts/native-ratchet.sh
  witness scripts/tests/native-ratchet-installed-files.sh checks executable files, hard links, symlinks and non-executable data are counted according to the installed-program budget
  source_path architecture/native-ratchet.cue
  source_path .githooks/pre-commit
  source_path .claude/hooks/native-ratchet.sh
  source_path .claude/hooks/institution-state.mjs
  source_path .github/workflows/native-ratchet.yml
  source_path docs/engineering/mjs-retirement-20261022/PLAN.md
  internal_calculus measure: authored .mjs files and lines (tracked or untracked, not ignored, vendored excluded), other scripts (.js .cjs .ts .tsx .py), bun build --compile sites outside comments, and, when ~/.bonfyre/bin exists, JS-runtime executables and the largest installed program
  internal_calculus check: cue vet of the measurement against #Measure; tighten: lower any budget to the current figure
  witness scripts/native-ratchet.sh check refused a one-line probe .mjs (files 1781 > 1780, lines over budget) and passes on the tree; 2026-10-22 figures went 1780 to 1778 files, 182482 to 176351 lines, 1 to 0 compile sites, 3 to 0 JS-runtime programs and 63.6 MB to 13.8 MB largest installed program
  invariant budgets only fall through tighten; raising one is a reviewed edit to architecture/native-ratchet.cue
  invariant the pre-commit hook, CI and Claude's PostToolUse hook on any script write all run the same check
  invariant an installed program in ~/.bonfyre/bin is never a packed JS runtime
  invariant installed program byte totals count regular executables once per inode and exclude symlinks and non-executable data files
  forbidden_inference a passing ratchet -> native, efficient or correct code; it counts files, lines and installed runtimes, not behaviour
  forbidden_inference fewer .mjs lines -> less functionality; ports are held to golden vectors so behaviour is kept while the JS goes
  known_gap other agents working in the tree add .mjs between measurements; the file budget is enforced at commit, so concurrent work must port or retire to land
  interacts ratchet-measures-retirement-archive
  source_lineage 2026-10-22 mjs retirement plan, docs/engineering/mjs-retirement-20261022

architecture js-compat-primitives
  canonical_name JsCompatPrimitives
  family optimization
  domain Optimization / Native port substrate
  layer substrate
  semantic_question What must C provide so a JS organ can be ported without changing a byte of its output, digests or receipts?
  purpose One shared substrate in libbonfyre for every JS-to-C port: a JSON writer byte-identical to JSON.stringify, a mutable JSON value with JS property order and canonical digests, and JS-compatible regular expressions
  maturity measured
  owns JsCompatibleEncoding
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/include/bf_jsonw.h
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/bf_jsonw.c
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/include/bf_jv.h
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/bf_jv.c
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/include/bf_re.h
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/bf_re.c
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/src/bf_sha256.c
  internal_calculus numbers: integers and short decimals by an exact Clinger fast path (N / 10^k equal to d with N under 10^15), else the shortest of 15, 16 or 17 significant digits that round-trips, subnormals searched in full; JS layout rules for exponents
  internal_calculus objects keep JS property order on insert (array-index keys first); digests are SHA-256 of a byte-sorted or a JS-sorted canonical form; objects past 16 keys get an open-addressed index
  internal_calculus regex: pattern to AST to a backtracking VM with a stack-allocated first frame, counted repetition expanded, progress checks on empty-capable loops, lookahead, ASCII case folding, whole code points for . and negated classes
  internal_calculus allocation: size-class free lists over 64 KiB slabs for values, keys and strings; SHA-256 on ARMv8 SHA instructions when present
  witness lib/libbonfyre/tests/bf_jsonw_parity.sh proves JSON.stringify layout, escapes, key order, canonical forms and digests equal Bun's, through both the writer and bf_jv
  witness lib/libbonfyre/tests/bf_re_parity.sh proves 51 patterns taken from the ports (lookahead, lazy, backreferences under i, multibyte quantifiers, replace templates) match Bun's RegExp offsets and replacements
  witness 2026-10-22: 300,000 random doubles of every magnitude format exactly as V8 prints them, and libm exp, log, log1p and expm1 agree with V8 bit for bit on 200,000 samples
  invariant ports compile with -ffp-contract=off: fused multiply-add changes the last bit of sums V8 computes unfused
  invariant a bf_jv tree belongs to one thread; the allocator is not thread-safe
  forbidden_inference a byte-identical port -> a correct organ; parity carries the old behaviour, mistakes included
  forbidden_inference bf_re -> full ECMAScript RegExp; lookbehind, named groups, unicode properties and the y and u flags are refused at compile
  known_gap key order for astral characters against U+E000..U+FFFF differs from UTF-16 sorting; no Bonfyre key uses them
  interacts decide-ports-on-js-compat-primitives
  source_lineage 2026-10-22 mjs retirement plan, WZ

architecture retirement-archive
  canonical_name RetirementArchive
  family optimization
  domain Optimization / Estate density
  layer storage
  semantic_question When code or a tree is retired, where does it go so nothing is lost and nothing stays behind?
  purpose Retire replaced source and cold trees into verified, path-ordered zstd archives with a sha256 manifest and a README entry, then remove them from the tree
  maturity measured
  owns RetiredArtifact
  source_path scripts/retire.sh
  internal_calculus every entry (symlinks and empty directories too) ordered by its path inside its top-level tree, tar --no-recursion, zstd -19 --long=27; restore proven by extraction, diff -r --no-dereference and the sha256 manifest before removal
  witness 2026-10-22 ~/.bonfyre/archive/retired: Downloads hand-off bundles 6,077 files 262 MB to 62 MB; Aurekai generated integration repos 649 files to 52 KB; operator TypeScript and the twelve DecisionPlane product files, each restore-verified before removal
  witness 2026-10-27 reference census (scripts, Makefiles, workflows, launchd, package files, C headers, pages, tests): 22 authored .mjs with no reference of any kind retired into js-unreferenced-20261027 (3,141 lines); four evidence copies of upstream Creator bytes into creator-upstream-copies-20261027
  witness 2026-10-27 maturity triage of test-only clusters: media-clip-review-20261027 (738 lines, orchestrator already gone), foreign-twin-fabric-20261027 (981 lines), research-consequence-prototype-20261027 (589 lines) and experience-handoff-protocol-20261027 (635 lines) retired with their own tests; none had an atlas entry, launchd, script or page caller. The Cloudflare admission path keeps experience-handoffs contract, artifacts, source-review-owner and handoff-fabric native-owner
  forbidden_inference an unreferenced file retired by census -> its capability was ported; it had no caller, and restoring it restores the same unwired code
  invariant nothing is removed unless the archive restores entry for entry
  invariant RETIRE_FROM retires outside the repo; the archive README names the restore command for each archive
  forbidden_inference a retired file -> a deleted capability; the capability moved to its native owner, and the source is restorable
  known_gap retiring live release trees under ~/.bonfyre/releases needs the owner's approval; 61 cold releases (1.04 GB) are listed in PLAN.md and not yet archived
  interacts ratchet-measures-retirement-archive
  source_lineage .claude/skills/density (ordering is the lever)

interaction ratchet-measures-retirement-archive
  source retirement-archive
  destination native-ratchet
  relation retired_sources_lower_the_measured_estate
  preserves restorable source bytes and the manifest of what left the tree
  drops the retired files from the measured estate
  forbidden_inference a lowered budget -> the retired code's behaviour is gone; it lives in its native owner and its archive
  invalidates_on retire.sh ordering or verification changing, or the ratchet's measured set changing
  witness scripts/retire.sh

interaction decide-ports-on-js-compat-primitives
  source cmd-books
  destination js-compat-primitives
  relation port_held_to_golden_vectors_through_shared_primitives
  preserves receipts, digests and printed output of the retired Bun products byte for byte, except tests/CORRECTIONS
  drops a JS runtime per product (three 63 MB executables became one 246 KB program)
  forbidden_inference golden parity -> new behaviour verified; only recorded behaviour is held
  invalidates_on bf_jsonw number or string formatting, bf_jv key order, bf_re semantics or the DecisionPlane CUE changing
  witness cmd/BonfyreDecide/tests/parity.sh
  binding lib/libbonfyre/bf_jv.c

architecture command-vectors
  canonical_name CommandVectors
  family optimization
  domain Optimization / Test estate
  layer verification
  semantic_question Which JS tests only spawn a native program and check what came back, and can their cases live as data replayed by one native runner?
  purpose Carry spawn-only JS test suites as bonfyre.command-vectors.v1 JSON beside the owning organ (ORGAN/tests/vectors/), replayed by one C runner, so the .mjs test can be retired without dropping an assertion
  maturity measured
  owns CommandVector
  source_path tests/vectors/bf_vectors.c
  source_path tests/vectors/Makefile
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tests/vectors/native_definition.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tests/vectors/native_resolution.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/tests/vectors/policy_compilation.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFinance/tests/vectors/zero_close.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFinance/tests/vectors/payment_options.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFinance/tests/vectors/supplier_quote_memo.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFinance/tests/vectors/relationship_states.json
  internal_calculus each case gets a fresh temporary directory and files; steps run a program with argv, env and stdin, then check exit, exact stdout or stderr, substrings, JSON deep equality, values at dotted paths (with * map and ?k=v selection), array membership, lengths, membership in a JSON file and file presence; SQLite setup and readback go through the sqlite3 program, so the runner owns no database code
  witness 2026-10-29 tests/vectors/bonfyre-vectors replays 7 vector files (24 cases, 1,769 checks) that carry 24 passing bun tests from BonfyreExperienceMap (native_definition, native_resolution, policy_compilation) and BonfyreFinance (zero_close, payment_options, supplier_quote_memo, relationship_states); mutated expectations fail; the 450 retired test lines are in experience-map-spawn-tests-20261029 and finance-spawn-tests-20261029
  forbidden_inference a passing vector set -> the program is correct; it answered the recorded inputs the way the retired assertions required, nothing more
  forbidden_inference a converted suite -> every JS test can become a vector; suites that build fault-injection binaries, race processes, compare against an independent encoder or read live stores stay as code
  invariant a .mjs test is retired only after its vectors pass against the same binary and every assertion it made is a check in a vector
  known_gap BonfyreCMS, BonfyreHash and components/BonfyreProject spawn suites need JSONL row selection, concurrency or fault-injection builds and are not converted; the runner is not yet run by CI
  interacts ratchet-measures-command-vectors
  interacts command-vectors-replay-admits-verified-repair
  internal_calculus repair replay (--replay-repair ID --case TEXT --before BIN --after BIN --runs N) replays one vector file N times through its binary_env against each binary and emits bonfyre.repair-replay.v1 with bf_jsonw; verdict replayed only when every before run fails a check of the named case, every after run passes the whole file, both sides' FAIL-location signatures are identical across runs and the two binaries differ in bytes
  witness 2026-10-30 packs/no-simulation/repair-replays-20261030/: 16 of the 19 repairs from the 2026-10-29 certification replayed 3x before (unmodified git 173d984a tree) and 3x after (working-tree build) with identical signatures; physics and discipl separated the binaries for a reason other than the claimed repair and wire's pre-fix tree passed, so all three are excluded (manifest.tsv)
  witness cmd/BonfyreCapability/tests/vectors/repair_admit.json runs the replay mode on toy programs: separated binaries replay; swapped, identical and wrong-case replays are not-replayed with their reasons
  forbidden_inference a replayed repair -> the two binaries differ only by that repair; the before tree is a commit, and its working-tree diff (hash recorded in before.source) can carry other changes
  forbidden_inference a replayed repair -> the repair is deployed, priced or a product; it says the vector separates two named binaries, nothing more
  source_lineage 2026-10-22 mjs retirement plan, W4

interaction ratchet-measures-command-vectors
  source command-vectors
  destination native-ratchet
  relation vectorized_tests_lower_the_measured_estate
  preserves every assertion of a retired spawn-only test as a vector check
  drops the .mjs test file and its Bun process
  forbidden_inference a lowered budget -> less test coverage; the checks moved into data replayed natively
  invalidates_on the runner's check semantics or the bonfyre.command-vectors.v1 shape changing
  witness tests/vectors/bf_vectors.c

interaction command-vectors-replay-admits-verified-repair
  source command-vectors
  destination cmd-capability
  relation deterministic_replay_gates_repair_record
  preserves the vector file sha256, the named case, run count, before and after binary sha256, the before source commit and diff hash, and each side's outcome signature
  drops per-run output text and the temporary case directories
  forbidden_inference an admitted repair record -> the installed organ carries the repair, an invocation is authorized, or a customer effect was verified
  invalidates_on the vector file or the after binary changing after the replay (admission re-hashes both and refuses), or the bonfyre.repair-replay.v1 shape changing
  witness cmd/BonfyreCapability/tests/vectors/repair_admit.json
